All six findings fixed, no gate weakened, no test deleted, no `#[ignore]`/`allow(` added.

## Fixes

**1. BLOCKER — `src/parser.rs:445`.** `module` added to `Parser::opens_block`, so nested module declarations spend the `MAX_BLOCK_DEPTH` budget. Reproduced first: 5000 nested `module` blocks aborted with `has overflowed its stack` (exit 134); 65 of them parsed with no error at all. Now 65 → `Blocks nest more than 64 levels deep` at the right span, and 5000 too.

**2. `src/vm.rs`.** `Vm` records every `module_member` name it publishes in a new `qualified_members` set (all three writers go through one `publish_member`), and `user_names` filters them. After `import MathUtils`, `:vars` no longer lists `MathUtils_circle_area`/`MathUtils_circle_circumference`/… and completion and the analyzer seed stop offering them; `MathUtils` and `TAU` are still there and `MathUtils.circle_area(2)` still runs. Consequence worth flagging: `say MathUtils_circle_area` is now `Unknown variable` in the REPL, which is what `rb run` has always said for a file.

**3. `src/repl/mod.rs:238`.** `:reset` moved into `reset_session`, which clears `multiline_buffer` and `in_multiline`. `repeat 3 times` → `:reset` → `say "hi"` now prints `hi`.

**4. `src/repl/mod.rs:606`.** `restore_session` now replays the restored lines through `execute_line` (so a multi-line block comes back whole) and reports how many were source vs. REPL commands. A restored command is listed, not re-run — otherwise the `:quit` in the saved file would end the session doing the restore. `set x to 1`/`:save`/fresh/`:restore`/`say x` → `1`.

**5. `src/repl/mod.rs:682`.** `:inspect` uses `Value::type_name()` (`number`, `text`, `list`, `function`), factored into `inspect_lines` so it is testable; `std::any::type_name_of_val` import dropped.

**6. `src/repl/commands.rs`.** `strip_prefix(SIGILS)` — exactly one sigil, so `::quit` is `Unknown command ':quit'` instead of quitting the session. The `.` sigil is now completed too (`ReplCommand::bare_names` + sigil-aware `complete_with`) and stated in `:help`.

